# Line endings in the files the tests read back.
#
# CI runs the suite on Windows as well as on Linux and macOS, and a Windows
# checkout converts a text file to CRLF by default. Three things in this
# repository read a file's bytes and compare them against something written
# here, so a converted checkout would fail them all in a way that looks like a
# language defect rather than a checkout setting:
#
#   - `miru fmt` writes `\n`, so a `.miru` file checked out with CRLF does not
#     round trip, and `tests/integration.rs` asserts that it does.
#   - `read_file` gives back exactly what is on disk, so `examples/words.txt`
#     with CRLF changes what `examples/words.miru` counts.
#   - The golden cases hold source text against output, character for character.
#
# Pinning these to LF everywhere is the fix. It is not a preference about
# editors: it is the condition under which the tests mean anything on Windows.
*.miru text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
*.rs text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf

# Binary, and never to be converted.
*.png binary
